#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1263 expect=violation domain=MB
#note "Was `valid_case_insensitive` (both exclusions folded). O-7 (Fix #338, ruling M2-D25) splits the two exclusions: MB.MBMETHOD is bound by the CDISC Library to codelist C85492 (METHOD) in SDTMIG 3.2/3.3/3.4 and GRAM STAIN is its submission value, so that exclusion is now exact; MBSTRESC binds no codelist anywhere, so NO GROWTH stays case-insensitive. Row 1: MBSTRESC 'no growth' still excludes the record -> silent. Row 2: MBMETHOD 'Gram Stain' is not the METHOD submission value, the exclusion does not apply, MBRESCAT is empty -> FIRES (the casing itself is CT2001's to report). Exactly one violation; a scenario silent on row 2 has re-introduced the fold, one firing on row 1 has dropped the MBSTRESC fold nobody ruled on."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=2 MBMETHOD="Gram Stain"
dataset MB class=FINDINGS label="Microbiology Specimen"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col MBSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col MBTESTCD type=Char label="Microbiology Test Short Name"
col MBSTRESC type=Char label="Character Result/Finding in Std Format"
col MBRESCAT type=Char label="Result Category"
col MBMETHOD type=Char label="Method of Test or Examination"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | MB | 01-701-1015 | 1 | ORGANISM | no growth     |  | CULTURE
CDISCPILOT01 | MB | 01-701-1015 | 2 | ORGANISM | GRAM POSITIVE |  | Gram Stain
